{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels","id":1028542,"title":"Spirits and health levels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T07:38:49-08:00","id":1028542,"title":"Spirits and health levels","content":"Here's some backstory, <br /> <br /> <br /> My dreamspeaker was attacked by 6th generation vampires, one a mesthulleh, the two other elders. The only defense he had was a materialized house spirit with rage 8, willpower 6, essence 70, power 54.<br /> <br /> The essence 70 was waived and 54 was played as the power. Despite what I understand in the book, I was told spirits had 7 health levels or so when they're materialized since they have the same health levels as corporate beings, and that they don't use their power/essence as health levels in the skinlands<br /> <br /> <br /> Needless to say, my character and the spirit died easily. My question is, was what was said about the health levels necessarily correct? This experience has kinda made me feel that dreamspeakers are useless, too<br /> <br /> <br /> My spheres at the moment(on this char):<br /> <br /> Spirit 3, prime 2, correspondence 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:17:27-08:00","id":1028555,"title":"","content":"To shed some light for the readers, you were attacked by 3 elders. Two of them were 6th generation vampires and one was a 7th generation, Not sure where you thought a ''mesthuelleh'' came into play but it seems like you're attempting to exaggerate the scene for some reason that I don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:48:58-08:00","id":1028564,"title":"","content":"One thing I need cleared up. How can your spirits have both a Power rating and an Essence rating? Those are supposed to be the same thing. Power is what WtA referred to it as, and it was change to Essence in Mage Revised at some point.<br /> <br /> Spirits should only have 4 base stats. Willpower, Rage, Gnosis, and Power/Essence.<br /> Anything else would just be Charms.<br /> <br /> Ok, so if your spirit was using Materialise, then yes, they have 7 health levels. But they can exchange essence for more health levels if they wanted to, either right of the bat to have a total of 10 or 20, or to &quot;heal&quot; lost health levels. It's part of the Materialise charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:54:57-08:00","id":1028569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028564#post1028564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I need cleared up. How can your spirits have both a Power rating and an Essence rating? Those are supposed to be the same thing. Power is what WtA referred to it as, and it was change to Essence in Mage Revised at some point.<br /> <br /> Spirits should only have 4 base stats. Willpower, Rage, Gnosis, and Power/Essence.<br /> Anything else would just be Charms.<br /> <br /> Ok, so if your spirit was using Materialise, then yes, they have 7 health levels. But they can exchange essence for more health levels if they wanted to, either right of the bat to have a total of 10 or 20, or to &amp;quot;heal&amp;quot; lost health levels. It's part of the Materialise charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see, I see. Would it be possible to infuse a spirit with more power levels (via prime sphere)<br /> <br /> Also, two more questions, are spirits supposed to use their charms in the skinlands? And two, does it make sense for a materialized spirit to guard a house if a shaman enters a pact with it to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:56:17-08:00","id":1028570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028555#post1028555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To shed some light for the readers, you were attacked by 3 elders. Two of them were 6th generation vampires and one was a 7th generation, Not sure where you thought a ''mesthuelleh'' came into play but it seems like you're attempting to exaggerate the scene for some reason that I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.... one of the 6th generation vampires could a Brujah embraced in Classical Athens by a fan of Socrates. That would could as a &quot;Methuselah&quot; to most vamps and would be unbelievably effective at causing massive property damage with Celerity and Potence..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:05:25-08:00","id":1028573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028569#post1028569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see, I see. Would it be possible to infuse a spirit with more power levels (via prime sphere)<br /> <br /> Also, two more questions, are spirits supposed to use their charms in the skinlands? And two, does it make sense for a materialized spirit to guard a house if a shaman enters a pact with it to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you certainly can use Prime to transfer Quintessence over from yourself over to the Spirit, and that would add to its power. However, I think it requires Prime 3 to do so.<br /> <br /> Spirits can do whatever the heck they want. They aren't like Wraiths who have laws against interfering with the land beyond the gauntlet. Some may argue they have more of a right to be on this side of the gauntlet that others.<br /> Whether they would guard the house in a pact made with the Shaman depends entirely one what kind of spirit they are, where their allegiances lie, and whether they respect the shaman enough to comply. Has the Shaman done something worthy of this spirits trust? What have the promised to do in exchange? That sort of stuff is important when dealing with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:14:28-08:00","id":1028576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028573#post1028573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you certainly can use Prime to transfer Quintessence over from yourself over to the Spirit, and that would add to its power. However, I think it requires Prime 3 to do so.<br /> <br /> Spirits can do whatever the heck they want. They aren't like Wraiths who have laws against interfering with the land beyond the gauntlet. Some may argue they have more of a right to be on this side of the gauntlet that others.<br /> Whether they would guard the house in a pact made with the Shaman depends entirely one what kind of spirit they are, where their allegiances lie, and whether they respect the shaman enough to comply. Has the Shaman done something worthy of this spirits trust? What have the promised to do in exchange? That sort of stuff is important when dealing with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, just wanted to know as these were things brought up during the scene by others that didn't make any sense. Thanks (:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:20:49-08:00","id":1028580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028573#post1028573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you certainly can use Prime to transfer Quintessence over from yourself over to the Spirit, and that would add to its power. However, I think it requires Prime 3 to do so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;re-tuning&quot; Quint into Essence officially takes Spirit as well. So it might be a Prime 3/Spirit 3. And Mages generally have less Quint on hand than spirits have Essence, so it might not be a cost effective action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:50:00-08:00","id":1028627,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers are far from useless. Spirit magic however is not the easiest to master, especially for new players. When your House Spirit alerted you to the presence of 3 elder vampires that weren't on the friends list there's a relative simple, although quite vulgar, course of action you could have taken with the spheres you listed.<br /> <br /> 1. Spirit 3 effect:: Step sideways into the Gauntlet - difficulty is local gauntlet level and it might take you a couple of turns to get enough successes but your house spirit should be able to keep them out for long enough by sealing the entrances shut.<br /> <br /> 2. Spirit 1 effect: Sense through the gauntlet - this way you can now see into your house, they will be hard pressed to see you<br /> <br /> 3. Spirit 2/Prime 2 effect: Infuse whatever weapon you have (even if its your damn shoe) with primal energy thus allowing it to inflict aggravated damage (1 quintessence per attack) and reach through the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Now you can attack the vampires as an invisible assailant unless they score enough successes to notice your presence before each attack with an Awareness Roll. You will be inflicting aggravated damage and there is doubtfully much they could do in return. Very few Vampires have abilities that can penetrate the gauntlet and there are even fewer that can do much more than look. Your House Spirit could use whatever charms it has to further impede them without materializing if able. If not no big deal. The vamps should be fleeing quickly once they realize they cant retaliate against you. If they do end up with some way to attack back it wont be very powerful and you can easily flee through the penumbra.<br /> <br /> I realize this is nice and all after the fact and doesn't really help your situation now, but hopefully it can come in handy in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:05:24-08:00","id":1028663,"title":"","content":"I'm the only one who's baffled by the whole situation?<br /> I don't know what baffles me more, the &quot;Three Elders enter in a house... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot; or that a <i>Disciple</i> (aka, a &quot;mage neonate&quot;) was deemed &quot;useless&quot; because wasn't able to kick their elderly asses...<br /> <br /> The strtategy suggested by Tuch it's a very strong one. Attacking from the Umbra it's one of the most infamous exploits that you can do agains't vampires. However, I find that the context it's a bit foggy...I mean, sure, there are few ways for vampires to attack the Umbra, but they aren't necesarily rarer than a Cotterie of Elders knocking your door...<br /> Without context, the whole situation sounds a bit like a <i>&quot;rock falls, you die&quot;</i> situation. How can we know that the player wasn't fighting the Storyteller himself?. Are all mage apprentices expected to survive an encounter like that!? (Because I would think not..). Was the player jumping at an impossible fight, without expecting what was going to happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-08-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:25:37-08:00","id":1028744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028627#post1028627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamspeakers are far from useless. Spirit magic however is not the easiest to master, especially for new players. When your House Spirit alerted you to the presence of 3 elder vampires that weren't on the friends list there's a relative simple, although quite vulgar, course of action you could have taken with the spheres you listed.<br /> <br /> 1. Spirit 3 effect:: Step sideways into the Gauntlet - difficulty is local gauntlet level and it might take you a couple of turns to get enough successes but your house spirit should be able to keep them out for long enough by sealing the entrances shut.<br /> <br /> 2. Spirit 1 effect: Sense through the gauntlet - this way you can now see into your house, they will be hard pressed to see you<br /> <br /> 3. Spirit 2/Prime 2 effect: Infuse whatever weapon you have (even if its your damn shoe) with primal energy thus allowing it to inflict aggravated damage (1 quintessence per attack) and reach through the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Now you can attack the vampires as an invisible assailant unless they score enough successes to notice your presence before each attack with an Awareness Roll. You will be inflicting aggravated damage and there is doubtfully much they could do in return. Very few Vampires have abilities that can penetrate the gauntlet and there are even fewer that can do much more than look. Your House Spirit could use whatever charms it has to further impede them without materializing if able. If not no big deal. The vamps should be fleeing quickly once they realize they cant retaliate against you. If they do end up with some way to attack back it wont be very powerful and you can easily flee through the penumbra.<br /> <br /> I realize this is nice and all after the fact and doesn't really help your situation now, but hopefully it can come in handy in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>My house spirit was materialized. Thing is, it has three charms, blast, materialize and airt sense. Needless to say, it wasn't very strong. One of the elders used a time effect to get 3 or so extra actions in the next four turns, so did another, so they attacked the spirit age skirted upstairs and stabbed me while I was trying to escape through the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:52:57-08:00","id":1028760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028744#post1028744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My house spirit was materialized. Thing is, it has three charms, blast, materialize and airt sense. Needless to say, it wasn't very strong. One of the elders used a time effect to get 3 or so extra actions in the next four turns, so did another, so they attacked the spirit age skirted upstairs and stabbed me while I was trying to escape through the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forge that spirits can also 