soak lethal quite easily (I only spent two essence points as opposed to three) then-.......yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:29:19-08:00","id":1028789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028770#post1028770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to attack with willpower then yeah, roll rage for damage, but when you're up against beings that can soak lethal quite easily (I only spent two essence points as opposed to three) then-.......yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you have used Prime 2 with Spirit 2 to &quot;Enchant&quot; the spirit, making all their attacks aggravated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:31:23-08:00","id":1028790,"title":"","content":"Yeah the spirit would have done better not materialized but oh well live and learn.<br /> <br /> Honestly I think I'm with Aleph on this one. I'm not exactly sure what a disciple level mage could have done to draw such attention from such a powerful hit squad. Either you really pissed off some vampire uppity up and you got a death sentence for character stupidity, and well shit happens. Or your ST grossly overestimated your character's strenght to deal with such a situation. <br /> <br /> The other possibility is what Aleph eluded to and that is a problem of a different kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:36:01-08:00","id":1028840,"title":"","content":"Now, would spirits that materialize via a fetish (like a guardian bear) be suspectible to the same kind of stuff? I.E, 7 health levels and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:47:06-08:00","id":1028842,"title":"","content":"See, this is the part that gets me and makes me wonder WTF happened to cause the scene...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>onedayumay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028555#post1028555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To shed some light for the readers, you were attacked by 3 elders. Two of them were 6th generation vampires and one was a 7th generation, Not sure where you thought a ''mesthuelleh'' came into play but it seems like you're attempting to exaggerate the scene for some reason that I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... How much exaggeration is really going on to say &quot;two were kinda old, one was really frelling old&quot; instead of &quot;all three were kinda old&quot;? To a newbie Mage, just getting his Mage on, is there even gonna be a difference here? It's splat all over his own upholstery either way. To say it's &quot;exaggerating the situation&quot; makes it sound like the ST was definitely railroading the situation, just not railroading it with extra railroads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:32:44-08:00","id":1028897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028840#post1028840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, would spirits that materialize via a fetish (like a guardian bear) be suspectible to the same kind of stuff? I.E, 7 health levels and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still need an answer to this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:05:37-08:00","id":1028954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028840#post1028840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, would spirits that materialize via a fetish (like a guardian bear) be suspectible to the same kind of stuff? I.E, 7 health levels and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can spend more Essence on the Materialize up front to gain more than HL.<br /> OTOH 1 Essence for the first 7 HL plus 1 for each further HL.<br /> Note, that HL and Size are somewhat related.<br /> Materialized Spirits can spend Essence in combat to heal as much HL as they like(1:1).<br /> Most Spirits can not gain Essence while materialized.<br /> If a spirit looses all his HL he is forced back in the penumbra, there he is free to do whatever he pleases (even to materialize again) IF he has Essence left (and enough of it to boot).<br /> IF the spirit looses the last HL and is forced into the Penumbra he must enter slumber to regain Essence at a rate of 1 point per hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:28:59-08:00","id":1029115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028542-spirits-and-health-levels?p=1028842#post1028842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is the part that gets me and makes me wonder WTF happened to cause the scene...<br /> <br /> I mean... How much exaggeration is really going on to say &quot;two were kinda old, one was really frelling old&quot; instead of &quot;all three were kinda old&quot;? To a newbie Mage, just getting his Mage on, is there even gonna be a difference here? It's splat all over his own upholstery either way. To say it's &quot;exaggerating the situation&quot; makes it sound like the ST was definitely railroading the situation, just not railroading it with extra railroads.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an entirely germane question to ask. The player shouldn't really be bummed that his &quot;attack dog&quot; house didn't obliterate the VASTLY SUPERIOR foes he was facing. It's almost unreasonable to expect a mage of that power facing vampires of that power to expect to live through the fight. The best hope might have been to throw the House in the way while trying to escape and praying that it was enough of an inconvenience to allow for the time to step sideways. That's the &quot;win&quot; in this scenario. And, depending on the vamps in question (as in, they have Celerity) it's probably not going to happen. However, that's if the fight just happened unexpectedly out of nowhere....<br /> <br /> As always, mages thrive on preparation. If the mage knew the vamps were coming, step sideways BEFORE they get there (Spirit 3). Awaken the House from the other side of the Gauntlet (Spirit 3) and have it try to pin the vamps inside it as long as possible. Summon other spirits that have Materialize Charms and make whatever fast and dirty deals needed to get them into the fray. (Spirit 2) (That one works better if your mage has the right spirits as buddies to begin with). Do it like a smart wizard from D&amp;D with Summon Monster spells, by using your Correspondence to keep a total awareness of where everyone is so the new spirits can be placed appropriately (in locations that keep the vampires inside your new buddy &quot;House&quot; and the can deal some damage). Still sitting pretty on the other side of the Gauntlet, use Prime to enchant some things for the spirits to pick up and use as weapons that do Aggravated Damage. (Spirit 2/Prime 2). Hell's bells, you could probably use Spirit 2 to grab one of those handy Primed up weapons yourself and start flailing away at the vamps while they can't reach you! (&quot;Why is there a flying, glowing baseball bat beating the crap out of me!?! And why does it <i>burn </i>so when it hits&quot; sayeth Vampire #2)<br /> <br /> The key might be just to immobilize them as long as possible. Like, say, until sunrise....<br /> <br /> Of course, your Paradox is going to build for most of that. But, if a low grade Disciple can even knock around some elder vamps and come away unscathed, that's a pretty significant accomplishment and is probably worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:00:27-08:00","id":1029131,"title":"","content":"These things happen because vampiric powers and magick work in very different ways. In the same vein, a strong Neonate can potentially kill a Master, if the mage is unprepared. Of course than a Master shouldn't be easy to caught unprepared, but then, neither should a group of alied Elders attack blindly a guy with supernatural powers (having no idea of what he can do, nor preparation against it)...<br /> In a normal situation, a starting mage character shouldn't be deemed &quot;useless in a fight&quot; just becuase he wasn't able to tank such enemies. But, in the end, all depends on context. I think this deserves a good talk between player and ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}